WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.025
Words in Context

00:00:02.405 --> 00:00:04.503
Predict your own word before you look.

00:00:05.703 --> 00:00:06.702
How to spot it

00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:08.959
A blank or an underlined word

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.014
Four single-word choices

00:00:11.565 --> 00:00:15.199
It’s testing: the precise meaning the context needs

00:00:16.399 --> 00:00:17.194
The method

00:00:17.594 --> 00:00:19.989
Step 1: Read the whole passage

00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:22.079
Not just the sentence with the blank.

00:00:22.629 --> 00:00:24.574
Step 2: Find the clue

00:00:24.854 --> 00:00:29.138
“But” and “although” flip the meaning. Colons and “because” match it.

00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:32.222
Step 3: Predict a simple word

00:00:32.502 --> 00:00:33.930
Say it in plain English.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.137
Step 4: Match it

00:00:36.417 --> 00:00:39.113
Check positive or negative, and how strong.

00:00:39.663 --> 00:00:40.773
In a few words

00:00:40.923 --> 00:00:43.008
Clue. Predict. Match.

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:45.113
Clue rules

00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:47.340
Contrast clues flip the meaning

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.670
although, but, while, yet

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.507
Right: Although the trail looked easy, it was strenuous.

00:00:54.057 --> 00:00:55.796
Restatement clues repeat it

00:00:56.076 --> 00:00:58.574
a colon, a dash, “that is”

00:00:58.854 --> 00:01:02.479
Right: She was considerate: she listened to everyone.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.398
Match the tone and strength

00:01:04.678 --> 00:01:07.137
“Not a compliment” needs a negative word.

00:01:07.687 --> 00:01:09.014
Beware the common meaning

00:01:09.294 --> 00:01:12.369
“Qualified” can mean “limited”, not “certified”.

00:01:13.569 --> 00:01:14.610
Let’s try one

00:01:15.022 --> 00:01:21.087
Although the scientist’s early experiments were ______, producing results that differed every time

00:01:21.087 --> 00:01:27.632
she repeated them, her later work was remarkably consistent and became a foundation for the field.

00:01:28.282 --> 00:01:33.493
Although sets up a contrast with her later work, which was remarkably consistent.

00:01:34.043 --> 00:01:38.601
And right after the blank: results that differed every time.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:41.461
So predict a simple word: unreliable.

00:01:42.011 --> 00:01:45.444
Influential, inexpensive, meticulous:

00:01:45.444 --> 00:01:49.572
none of them mean unreliable. Inconsistent does.

00:01:49.572 --> 00:01:50.429
Choice A.

00:01:51.629 --> 00:01:52.625
Common traps

00:01:53.025 --> 00:01:54.033
The common meaning

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:56.598
The obvious definition is often the trap.

00:01:57.148 --> 00:01:58.226
The topic word

00:01:58.506 --> 00:02:01.261
Sounds related. Doesn’t fit the logic.

00:02:02.461 --> 00:02:03.885
Words in Context

00:02:04.165 --> 00:02:06.251
Clue. Predict. Match.

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:07.574
Spot it

00:02:07.774 --> 00:02:10.926
Blank or underlined word + 4 single words

00:02:11.476 --> 00:02:12.184
Steps

00:02:12.384 --> 00:02:14.189
1. Read the whole passage

00:02:14.469 --> 00:02:15.899
2. Find the clue

00:02:16.179 --> 00:02:18.453
3. Predict your own simple word

00:02:18.733 --> 00:02:21.472
4. Match meaning, direction, strength

00:02:22.022 --> 00:02:22.774
Remember

00:02:22.974 --> 00:02:25.792
although / but / while → opposite meaning

00:02:26.072 --> 00:02:29.119
colon / dash / that is → same idea

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:32.378
Match the tone: positive or negative

00:02:32.658 --> 00:02:35.583
Underlined word: beware the common meaning

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:36.738
Trap

00:02:36.938 --> 00:02:39.327
The topic word that only sounds related

00:02:40.077 --> 00:02:43.772
